.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-RENAME" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-rename - Rename a machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine rename <machine> <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename a machine, selected by its current name or ID. The new name must follow the machine
name rules; a refused name is explained without echoing what you typed. Its ID and grants
stay as they are. Afterwards the local machine list refreshes, so the new name resolves at once.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rename

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb machine rename old-name db-1
  pb machine rename m_abc123 db-1 --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
